Rules of Exception Law

1. Logic Puzzle, "For every exception there is an exception, except the exception.".

2. How exception theory came to be, "It started with 'For every exception there is and exception.'. Which then logically led to 'except the exception'. Then came a question; how many of those "except the exception"'s 'exception' are there? It was a hard thing to figure out and crack. Then, Exception Theory became what you see. It was all derived from that.

3. P is for Point, it is the substrate. The ultimate Point is the total set of infinities, Absolute Infinity.

4. D is for Descriptor, it describes. The ultimate Descriptor is the total set of finite, Absolute Finite.

5. T is for Traverser, it traverses. The ultimate Traverser is the total set of indeterminate, Absolute Indeterminate.

6. The binding and interaction are the same, so Binding/Interaction. It is inherent and intrinsic.

7. 'Something' and its parts, everything and anything, is relational. There is only pure relativism.

8. E is for 'Something'. 'Something' is everything and anything. 'Something' is comprised of PDT. PDT generates 'Something'. Outside of 'Something' is still 'Something'.

9. E = (P°D°T)

10. (P°D)°T or T°(P°D) as the T placement does not matter. There can never be (D°P) as a Descriptor must describe a Point.

11. "True" Absolute Nothing cannot exist. The moment it can have a name means it can be described and thus it is 'Something'. One can only attach 'Something' to it, this leads to there always being 'Something'.






























